WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.267
-"Sing 2" is coming out
next week.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.200
I mean, we're excited
about this.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.100
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.934
It has such an amazing cast

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.634
and we wanted to do something
fun with the actors,

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.868
so we gave them a bunch
of weird phrases

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.601
and asked them
to sneak those phrases

00:00:12.601 --> 00:00:15.434
into their interviews
as casually as possible.

00:00:15.434 --> 00:00:17.434
No one knew we were doing this.
So, check it out.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.734
It's time for "Drop It In."

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.734
-♪ Drop It In, Drop It In ♪

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:24.667
♪ D-D-D-D-Drop It In, yeah ♪

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:27.968
-Obviously, everyone's going
to watch "Sing 2" for Christmas.

00:00:27.968 --> 00:00:28.968
How do you guys plan

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:31.234
on celebrating Christmas
this year?

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:34.167
-I'm just going to eat
a lot of food, I feel like,

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.300
'cause, you know...

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.234
[ Ding ]
...you know?
-That's right.

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.234
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Which of the following

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.901
is not a marsupial --

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:46.701
kangaroo, koala, or platypus?

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:49.501
-Koala.
-Platypus have no pouches.

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.200
They're the only
egg-laying mammal.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.000
-Pouches, eggs...

00:00:57.234 --> 00:00:59.200
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.267
Yeah.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:03.267
-I think it's also a movie
about...

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:07.634
overcoming your own
personal obstacles and --

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.067
I mean...

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:11.968
-How many "Sing" stories

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.334
do you want to tell?
Like have you thought

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.901
of what you would write
for "Sing 3" or "Sing 4"?

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.000
..."Sing 8," yeah...

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.400
-It'd be like the KIDZ BOP
version of movies!

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.567
-..."12." Yeah! I mean,
you'd skip 13 because of,

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.400
you know, bad vibes.
-Yeah, no, you can never
do that.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:31.267
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:32.300
-But, no, I think, otherwise,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.667
it could go on forever.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:37.300
-So, this was obviously
like filming during the pand--

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.934
Did you guys get to get together
at any point?
-Ugh!

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.234
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:46.234 --> 00:01:47.567
They're grape!

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:49.300
-That's sort of the fun
of show business

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.767
and the hard part is, you know,

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:53.901
you get ready and then there's
someone who can tell you no

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:56.467
and it's deflating, you know?

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.200
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]
...and I think that the beauty

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.534
of this cast of characters is
they don't stop.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.434
-In the film, Buster Moon has
to tell a little white lie.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.133
I'm curious to know
if you've ever had to exaggerate

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.767
a special skill to either land
a role or get ahead.

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:15.000
-I never will tell a white lie.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.868
And that's something I learned
when I once

00:02:18.868 --> 00:02:21.267
put a balloon
inside of a microwave and...

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.167
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.167 --> 00:02:27.334
I just have
one last thing to say.

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:30.901
Nunca es un buen idea poner
un globo en el microondo.

00:02:30.901 --> 00:02:32.334
[ Ding ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.701
And that's something that is
really important to remember.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.801
-[ Laughs ] Thank you
for sharing that tip with us.

